    [Doc][Misc] Add release note fragment for PR 19395 (#20333)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Adds the missing release note fragment for PR #19395. It records the
    Model Runner V2 EPLB deprecation and unsupported configuration handling
    so the release note tooling can include it.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No runtime or configuration change.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Ran git diff --check
    - Parsed elease_notes/fragments/19395.yaml with PyYAML
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/544f182d9f0c9bfe8bd7645525951d5e3692a542
    
    Signed-off-by: x00946744 <xingbowen1@huawei.com>
    Co-authored-by: x00946744 <xingbowen1@huawei.com>

diff --git a/release_notes/fragments/19395.yaml b/release_notes/fragments/19395.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..c2c12594d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/release_notes/fragments/19395.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+pr: 19395
+entries:
+  - category: breaking
+    text: >-
+      Deprecated the Model Runner V1 EPLB environment switches
+      `DYNAMIC_EPLB` and `EXPERT_MAP_RECORD` for Model Runner V2.
+      Model Runner V2 now warns and ignores these switches; use
+      `--enable-eplb` and `--eplb-config` instead.
+  - category: config
+    text: >-
+      Model Runner V2 now warns and filters unsupported
+      `additional_config.eplb_config` and `stair_config` fields instead of
+      failing at startup, while preserving supported values.
